== Mock Examination 2 — Questions

#mcq(1, [A lichen is best described as a partnership between], [two fungi], [an alga and a fungus], [a bacterium and a virus], [a moss and an alga])

#mcq(2, [An organ is best defined as], [a group of identical cells], [a single specialised cell], [a group of organs working together], [a group of tissues working together for a particular function])

#mcq(3, [In a flowering plant, the cells produced by meiosis in the anther are], [pollen grains carrying the haploid number of chromosomes], [diploid cells that divide by mitosis to make leaves], [xylem vessels], [root hair cells])

#mcq(4, [The air spaces of the spongy mesophyll are important because they], [store starch], [contain chlorophyll], [let carbon dioxide diffuse quickly to the cells], [prevent water loss])

#mcq(5, [Vitamin A deficiency causes], [rickets], [beri-beri], [night blindness], [scurvy])

#mcq(6, [Water enters a root hair cell by], [active transport], [diffusion of water through the xylem only], [transpiration pull directly], [osmosis])

#mcq(7, [Lymph differs from blood in that lymph], [has no red blood cells], [contains more oxygen], [is pumped by the heart], [contains no white cells])

#mcq(8, [Which pair of organs is directly involved in the excretion of carbon dioxide?], [Kidneys and liver], [Lungs and gills], [Skin and kidneys], [Liver and lungs])

#mcq(9, [The kidneys remove urea because urea is], [undigested protein], [a nitrogenous waste formed in the liver from excess amino acids], [a hormone], [a vitamin])

#mcq(10, [Which of these is NOT a function of the human skeleton?], [Protection of organs], [Support of the body], [Production of digestive enzymes], [Provision of a surface for muscle attachment])

#mcq(11, [Which of these diseases is *not* caused by a virus?], [Poliomyelitis], [Rabies], [Influenza], [Cholera])

#mcq(12, [The presence of circular DNA and 70S ribosomes in mitochondria is used as evidence that mitochondria], [were once free-living bacteria], [are made by the Golgi body], [have no function], [contain chlorophyll])

#mcq(13, [Tumour cells are dangerous mainly because they], [stop dividing], [lose their cell walls], [divide repeatedly without control], [become haploid])

#mcq(14, [On a graph of the rate of photosynthesis against light intensity, the point at which the curve first levels off marks], [the temperature optimum], [the compensation point], [the death of the leaf], [the intensity at which light stops being the limiting factor])

#mcq(15, [Roughage (dietary fibre) is important because it], [adds bulk that stimulates peristalsis], [supplies energy], [builds muscle], [is absorbed as glucose])

#mcq(16, [Stomata are described as pores with guard cells because], [they are always open], [the two guard cells can change shape and open or close the pore], [they are plugged by wax], [they have no relation to the pore])

#mcq(17, [The 'double circulation' of a mammal means that], [there are two hearts], [blood passes through the heart twice for every complete circuit], [blood flows in two directions], [there are two aortas])

#mcq(18, [Inhaled air differs from exhaled air in that inhaled air contains], [more carbon dioxide and more water vapour], [less oxygen and more nitrogen], [more oxygen and less carbon dioxide], [the same gases in the same proportions])

#mcq(19, [The blood leaving the kidney is different from the blood entering it because it contains], [less urea and less water], [more urea], [more glucose], [more red cells])

#mcq(20, [The number of bones in the adult human skeleton is], [300], [150], [66], [206])

#mcq(21, [Which of these ranks is the largest?], [Order], [Class], [Family], [Species])

#mcq(22, [A cell placed in a concentrated sugar solution will], [lose water and become plasmolysed], [gain water and become turgid], [stay unchanged], [burst])

#mcq(23, [Asexual reproduction is advantageous to a plant living in a stable habitat because it], [creates new gene combinations every time], [always produces disease resistance], [reduces the population], [quickly produces many offspring of a proven successful type])

#mcq(24, [Chlorophyll is located in the], [cell wall], [nucleus], [thylakoid membranes of the chloroplast], [mitochondria])

#mcq(25, [The dental formula of an adult human is], [2.2.2.3 / 2.1.2.3], [2.1.2.3 / 2.1.2.3], [3.1.2.2 / 3.1.2.2], [2.1.3.3 / 2.1.3.3])

#mcq(26, [Xylem vessels are well adapted to their function because they are], [living, narrow and full of cytoplasm], [dead with sieve plates], [dead, hollow and strengthened with lignin], [living with many mitochondria])

#mcq(27, [Which vessel has the thickest, most elastic muscular wall?], [The vena cava], [A capillary], [The pulmonary vein], [The aorta])

#mcq(28, [The breathing centre that controls the rate of breathing is in the], [medulla oblongata], [cerebrum], [cerebellum], [hypothalamus])

#mcq(29, [Selective reabsorption in the nephron returns to the blood], [glucose, amino acids and most of the water and salts], [all the urea], [blood cells], [large proteins])

#mcq(30, [The bones of the digits are called], [carpals], [tarsals], [metacarpals], [phalanges])

#mcq(31, [Which feature is absent from all members of the kingdom Fungi?], [A cell wall], [Chlorophyll], [A nucleus], [Spores])

#mcq(32, [Which statement about the cell membrane is correct?], [It is made of cellulose and is fully permeable], [It is a rigid layer of chitin], [It is made of protein and lipid and is selectively permeable], [It has no control over movement of substances])

#mcq(33, [Independent assortment of chromosomes takes place during], [anaphase of mitosis], [prophase II], [metaphase I], [cytokinesis])

#mcq(34, [Which of these is *not* a fate of the glucose made in photosynthesis?], [Conversion to starch for storage], [Excretion through the stomata], [Conversion to sucrose for transport], [Use in the manufacture of cellulose])

#mcq(35, [A carnivore's dentition is characterised by], [large pointed canines and carnassial teeth for shearing], [broad ridged molars for grinding], [a gap between incisors and premolars], [continuously growing incisors])

#mcq(36, [A potometer is used to], [measure photosynthesis], [collect oxygen], [measure humidity], [measure the rate of water uptake by a shoot as a measure of transpiration])

#mcq(37, [A person with blood group AB can receive blood from any group because their red cells], [have both A and B antigens and the plasma has no antibodies], [have no antigens], [have no antibodies in their red cells], [do not clump])

#mcq(38, [The site of the reactions of the Krebs cycle is the], [cytoplasm], [nucleus], [matrix of the mitochondrion], [cell membrane])

#mcq(39, [Excretion differs from secretion because excretion], [is carried out only by glands], [removes metabolic waste from the body], [always produces hormones], [removes undigested food])

#mcq(40, [The joint at the shoulder is a], [hinge joint], [gliding joint], [sutured joint], [ball-and-socket joint])

